import urllib.request, json, pathlib, os
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
prompt="""You are GPT-6.2-astra, CAD geometry expert. Source image lamp actual proportions: 380mm long zeppelin, only 105mm high body, strong asymmetric top shell 65mm ABOVE central rod and bottom shell 40mm BELOW. At 9 positions x=-166,-124,-82,-41,0,41,82,124,166 and center rail Z=102, broad overlapping satin silver curved louver scoops each rigidly mounted on its Y-directed pivot. Panel halfwidths [25,37,47,51,57,51,47,37,25]mm. Top heights [20,33,47,58,65,58,47,33,20] and bottom heights [16,25,32,37,40,37,32,25,16]. OLD MODEL flat vertical elliptic paddles looked like stacks of paper; new model must resemble aerodynamic Zeppelin metallic scalloped, curved metal, overlapped shell with smooth concave gradations. User requires REAL CadQuery / Blender CAD renders, no generated images.
Write only a compact complete valid Python function make_louver(halfwidth, up, down, side, layer) returning a watertight CadQuery Solid, using import cadquery as cq, import math. LOCAL coordinates: X horizontally, Y depth front side=-1, Z vertical around pivot at (0,0,0). Plate thickness 0.6mm. Make at least 36 sections; each section is a 4-corner wire for Solid.makeLoft(... ruled=True). Its front face is CYLINDRICALLY curved (developable because Y depends ONLY on X, not Z), inward/outward sag 8-12mm across X, with peak ellipse vertical halfheight up/down*sqrt(1-(x/halfwidth)^2). The metal face must have rounded smooth shape, visible specular gradient, no sharp waist notches and no visible screw row. Avoid degenerate loft sections at tips by clipping fraction to .994. Use 3D thickness normal along Y/X chord, and create a tiny center through-hole around local pivot using cylindrical cutter radius 2.7 axis +Y if feasible. It must be robust as cq.Solid for 9 geometries x 2 sides. If loft invalid, use CQ solids robust version. Do not generate separate light mesh in this function. Output Python code only, no explanations, no markdown. It will be embedded into a larger mechanical CAD build."""
body={"model":"gpt-6.2-astra","reasoning":{"effort":"high"},"max_output_tokens":4800,"input":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":prompt}]}]}
req=urllib.request.Request("https://api.openai.com/v1/responses",data=json.dumps(body).encode(),headers={"Authorization":"Bearer "+os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"],"Content-Type":"application/json"},method="POST")
try:
 with urllib.request.urlopen(req,timeout=200) as r: response=json.load(r)
 code="\n".join(part.get("text","") for msg in response.get("output",[]) for part in msg.get("content",[]) if part.get("type")=="output_text")
 if code.lstrip().startswith(chr(96)*3):code=code.strip().split("\n",1)[1].rsplit(chr(96)*3,1)[0]
 (p/"astra_louver.py").write_text(code,encoding="utf-8")
 print(json.dumps({"model":response.get("model"),"status":response.get("status"),"code_chars":len(code),"usage":response.get("usage"),"start":code[:280]},ensure_ascii=True),flush=True)
except urllib.error.HTTPError as e: print("API_HTTP_ERROR",e.code,e.read(700).decode(errors="replace"),flush=True)
except Exception as e: print("API_ERROR",type(e).__name__,str(e)[:300],flush=True)
